test.yaml:8:14: free text of an outsider from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is expanded into the program of sed: a value with a slash ends the command and the rest is a program of its own. GNU sed runs commands with `e` (`a/g;1e id;#`) and writes files with `w`. keep the value out of the program text: read it from the environment in awk (ENVIRON["BODY"]) or perl ($ENV{BODY}), or cut it down to letters and digits first [argument-injection]
